# Redirects for the landing page.
#
# cmd/dessau-site copies this file to the ROOT of the output directory as
# `_redirects`, beside `_headers`, which is where the host reads it: one list
# for the whole assets directory, while the page itself is served from a path
# under it.
#
# A superseded path that no Worker is attached to cannot be redirected at all —
# the request is answered by the apex before anything here sees it. So
# wrangler.jsonc routes the old path to this Worker for no reason but these two
# lines: it is claimed in order to be given away again.
#
# 301 and not 302: the old path is not coming back, and a permanent code is
# what lets a browser and a search index stop asking for it.
#
# Two rules and not one, because a splat does not match the empty string: on
# its own the second rule leaves the bare path unredirected, which is the
# spelling a person types. `:splat` carries whatever followed the slash to the
# same place under the current path, so a deep link keeps its destination.

/Gropius        /Dessau/        301
/Gropius/*      /Dessau/:splat  301
